WEBVTT

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:24.990
Having one talent too many is more dangerous than having one talent too few. -Nietzsche

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:32.510
There's something frightening about anyone who can
consciously, intentionally trample others underfoot.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.010
Is there?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.050
I'm far more frightened of those who unconsciously,

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:48.360
unintentionally trample others, those who trample
others in the name of what's right and what's just.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:53.570
Oh? Ha. So you're a good guy, then.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:59.740
Most likely this isn't a difference of opinion
so much as a difference in how we live.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:04.570
The absolute, fundamental division between those who live without

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:09.170
the need to trample others, and those who don't even rate a trampling.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.090
That's all.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.930
Like the artist with no style.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.760
Like the academic with nothing else to achieve.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.810
Like the cook who had mastered all flavors.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.680
Like the fortune teller who had divined too much.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:28.980
The women on that island were on the other side of that divide.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:35.950
This is a question of what a genius is, and what a genius isn't.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.820
There are two fundamental ways to live.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:49.330
Live mindful of how little you matter, or live
mindful of how little the world matters. Just those two.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:55.840
Allow the world to rob you of your value,
or destroy the world and make it yours.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.850
You have to decide to value yourself, or to value the world.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.350
Is the world boring, or are you? Which is better?

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.860
Where does genius begin, and where does it end?

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.230
Well? What say you?

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.610
Well...

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.860
How do you view the world?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.120
But I'd already been through the events on that island.
I had been by the side of the blue savant.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:34.500
I had spoken to the person in front of me.
So I knew better than to consider the answer.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.760
It was all just nonsense.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.880
So I said nothing.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.430
Instead, I looked away, and thought of something else.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.690
Of how the world might look in her eyes.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:56.570
Of how she might see me.

