00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:56.390
Were you being coy? Just in case you've
got the wrong idea, I'm not really that important.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:16:02.900
No, it's just...I was in the program, but I dropped out.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:07.400
It's still pretty impressive. Even if you did take a sabbat, you still вЂ“

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:08.400
Sabbatical.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:15.870
A sabbatical, you still passed the ER3 entrance exam,
which is no joke. Getting in's a real achievement.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:19.870
You should be proud of that, I think.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:25.290
If you drop out, it means nothing. In this world, results are everything.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:29.170
I think everything is a result.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.170
Sorry for the wait!

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.270
So what is your relationship with Kunagisa?

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:47.940
I met her before I joined the program.

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:50.070
So about five years ago.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:57.410
And when you came back, she was a cyberterrorist! Shocking.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.200
My relationship with Kunagisa...

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:05.830
Is not something I can easily answer questions about.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.880
She needs me. I know that much.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:14.090
But it didn't need to be me.

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:18.470
It's rather difficult to explain why that should be.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:24.480
And it would involve a number of private things about her, so I preferred to avoid it altogether.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:29.360
I haven't talked with her much...

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:34.240
But she has a few too many flaws to lead a normal life.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.320
Maybe flaws isn't the word.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.580
She isn't diminished by them in any way.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:45.620
But the way she concentrates is not very balanced.

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:50.250
Reminded me of some kids I know with savant syndrome.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:52.000
Savant.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.800
French for 'learned'.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:18:00.470
I knew that Kunagisa had once been called a savant.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:05.560
I knew that only too well.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.810
You know the rules to shogi or chess at least?

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:16.530
Why not play a game with me?
We can reminisce about ER3 while we play.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.280
Sure...but not blindfolded.

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:21.370
I've got a board in my room.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:26.580
I have a little work to wrap up in the morning,
so how about you come by after lunch?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.330
Sure. Oh...wait, sorry, I can't.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.000
Prior appointment.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.880
A prior...oh, with Kunagisa?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.720
-Then no help for it.
-No, with Kanami...

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:43.430
Since we have no small connection between us,
allow me to give you this warning.

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:47.270
You should spend no time with anyone in such a base occupation.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.440
Akane, you really don't like Kanami, do you?

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:56.440
That's not it. I have no basis for any
strong opinions about the woman herself.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:19:00.200
But artists are the scum of the earth.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.030
Hmph.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:04.950
Ah...sorry.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:12.830
I said too much. I don't take it back,but
it's never fun hearing someone gripe about others.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:15.750
I'd better clear my head.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.100
Good morning!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:28.600
Hey.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.150
That's no way to greet someone this early.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.690
Not that I'm early!

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.280
Himena Maki.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.360
cover this uuuup

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.360
and this 22

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.360
Genius Fortune Teller

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.360
Himena Maki

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.070
She was a genius fortune teller.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:49.500
She worked for governments and corporations,
acting less like a fortune teller and more like a cult leader,

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:53.960
using her talents without drawing attention to herself.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.710
Some people even say she's an oracle!

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:05.640
Her powers let her see the past, the future,
know people, the world, and everything!

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.510
Powers?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:08.930
Psychic powers!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:15.520
Maki's abilities would be..retrocognition; precognition, and telepathy.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:20.780
So my being a fortune teller...doesn't sit well with you.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:25.030
No...it's fine.

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:27.160
Yeah. I know.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:32.290
Whatever...you don't matter.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:33.830
I don't?

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:37.290
Mm. You're the Japanese representative for not mattering.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:42.800
But out of the goodness of my heart, I will give you one warning.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:46.760
Your impression of me is fundamentally wrong.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.560
And not just me.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:55.900
Your impressions of everyone on this island are all wrong.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:59.150
And that includes Kunagisa.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:06.780
It's like you are deliberately twisting your values when dealing with other people.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:13.330
That can make it easier to go through life,
but I wouldn't call it a very smart choice to make.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:16.580
Eventually, it will backfire. Be careful.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:25.050
Like she really was telepathic, everything
Maki said hit way too close to home.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:30.970
Honestly? I thought she was creepy.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:32.970
Sorry to be creepy.

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:43.360
Oh, Ii-chan. You're back. Well? Meet anyone?

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:48.620
I met almost everyone. Only people I haven't seen today are...lesse...

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:53.870
Teruko and Ilia. Oh, right, also Yayoi.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.630
So almost perfect!

00:21:58.830 --> 00:21:59.580
Hunh?

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:05.880
Perfect score in the contest to meet everyone
on Wet Wing Raven Island this morning!

00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:10.640
Ii-chan, your watch is broken.

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:15.390
Gimme. I'll fix it!

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:22.900
2nd Floor, Ibuki Kanami's Room

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:29.660
Um...Kanami.

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:32.120
Aren't you...going to draw?

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:33.910
I'm busy memorizing you.

00:22:34.200 --> 00:22:35.370
Haven't you heard?

00:22:35.870 --> 00:22:38.460
I only work when I'm alone.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:42.670
Can't concentrate when people are around.

00:22:43.840 --> 00:22:48.220
When I do portraits, I have to rely entirely on my memories.

00:22:48.220 --> 00:22:50.430
You can do that?

00:22:50.590 --> 00:22:53.560
With me, memory and perception are one and the same.

00:22:53.890 --> 00:22:59.060
If we talk like this for a couple of hours,
you can leave, and I'll paint the portrait.

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:01.350
Is that...?

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:05.110
When did you draw that?

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:08.320
This morning. Got a problem with that?

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:15.950
Only idiots take three or four months to do something they can finish in a week.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:18.460
Idiots, or the lazy.

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:23.340
So tell me...what did you think of this picture?

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:24.710
Well, um...

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:26.960
I guess...

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:29.380
It's very pretty.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:32.590
Pretty, hunh?

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:38.520
I'm not after flattery. I won't get mad at you or anything.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:44.610
Right, but...I don't have the eye of a critic. I'm no judge of art.

00:23:45.440 --> 00:23:48.110
I just thought it was pretty.

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:50.900
Pretty.

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:55.870
Pretty. Pretty, pretty, pretty.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:00.370
That's not a word any artist wants to hear.

00:24:03.880 --> 00:24:05.290
What are you doing!?

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:08.050
Destroying a failed work, obviously.

00:24:10.510 --> 00:24:12.760
What's the use?

00:24:14.300 --> 00:24:15.140
Seriously.

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:18.890
Could have been worth twenty million, too.

00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:20.350
Twenty million yen?

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:21.480
Dollars.

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:28.530
You shouldn't feel guilty. The fault is mine.

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:33.200
I am not foolish enough to put the blame for my own failures on others.

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:38.490
But I don't know what I'm talking about! What does my opinion matter?

00:24:38.490 --> 00:24:43.160
If you have to choose your judges, it is not worth calling art.

00:24:44.920 --> 00:24:49.170
By the way, I heard you and Akane don't get along.

00:24:49.170 --> 00:24:50.420
We don't.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:54.430
At least, she certainly seems to hate me.

00:24:54.760 --> 00:25:08.690
Personally, I intend to continue respecting Sonoyama as
an academic, as a researcher, and as one of the Seven Fools.

00:25:08.690 --> 00:25:13.650
You intend? But in actual fact...?

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:18.410
Sonoyama Akane herself, I absolutely despise.

00:25:44.890 --> 00:25:50.360
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:25:50.360 --> 00:25:53.780
Spun around when near you

00:25:53.990 --> 00:25:57.160
Leaning towards your right

00:25:57.160 --> 00:25:59.620
What I've got in my hands

00:25:59.620 --> 00:26:02.490
Is not a dream or nothing

00:26:02.490 --> 00:26:06.160
But there's something somewhere

00:26:06.160 --> 00:26:09.210
Throbbing in my heart

00:26:09.210 --> 00:26:12.130
If the one that you do love

00:26:12.130 --> 00:26:16.470
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:19.260
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:26:19.260 --> 00:26:23.520
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:26.060
We'd once been so hollow

00:26:26.060 --> 00:26:28.900
Trapped inside that little box

00:26:28.900 --> 00:26:32.400
But now we've seen outside that box

00:26:32.400 --> 00:26:35.650
And have no idea where we are.

00:26:36.070 --> 00:26:37.490
That's all.

00:26:51.380 --> 00:26:53.920
Afterimages of our bliss

00:26:53.920 --> 00:26:56.710
Glimpses of the future

00:26:56.710 --> 00:27:00.340
A glance at something fragile

00:27:00.340 --> 00:27:05.180
Those times that we can still laugh together
